 ## Background
-Instanced rendering originated as a technique to optimize rendering of large numbers of static objects like terrain chunks, leaves, and trees [S5, unofficial]. It was developed to address performance bottlenecks of traditional per-object rendering where each object requires a separate draw call and state change [S2, unofficial][S6, unofficial]. The technique leverages GPU hardware capabilities to iterate over instance data efficiently [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial]. It is widely used in voxel engines and large-scale scene rendering [S3, unofficial][S4, unofficial].
